0	196	Michaele Schreyer (born 9 August 1951) is a German politician of Alliance 90/The Greens who served as a European Commissioner from September 1999 to November 2004, holding the budget portfolio.



196	291	Education
Schreyer wrote her doctoral thesis on tax federalism at the University of Cologne.



291	439	Political career
From 1983 until 1987, Schreyer worked as an advisor on financial policy to the Green Party's parliamentary group in the Bundestag.

439	569	In 1989, Schreyer was appointed State Minister for Urban Development in the government of Governing Mayor Walter Momper of Berlin.
570	649	In the 1990 state elections, she was elected to the Abgeordnetenhaus of Berlin.
650	737	Between 1995 and 1997, she served as chairwoman of the Sub-Committee on Public Housing.
738	1056	In 1998, she assumed the leadership of the Green Party's parliamentary group, alongside Renate Künast.


